From 31dd6d39f8c90b90967f82566b597ccc476b8394 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:14:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Project current-run replica evidence on primary
 boards

Why: primary sync mode correctly refuses local observation authority, but local card lists, counts and detail had no replica evidence path. Every running card therefore became unknown. Remote rows already use executor-stamped current-run events. Reuse that evidence contract for primary reads only, with portable run identity, matched task/run and expiry. Never derive liveness from a pull clock or task heartbeat. Mirrored heartbeat columns are absent on real running rows; synced executor events carry the clock.

Proof: initial regression RED (running became unknown, heartbeat clock absent); 75 consumer files / 1051 tests pass, focused final 55 tests pass, scripts/check passes. Nine targeted guard/path mutants killed after adding a missing current-run join control. List/count parity, detail, unknown mode, missing/foreign/ended run, missing/malformed event, preserved human request, expiry, OFF/SHADOW and remote controls. Live hub read-only inspection confirmed portable current run UIDs and executor heartbeat events with NULL mirrored heartbeat columns. Deployment and Desktop readback remain post-landing gates.
